cast: kemi

== room | SNOWY NIGHT · DORM ROOM | small dorm room at night with snow falling outside the window and warm lights | phone
kemi (worried): Quddus, it's snowing, I'm cold, and I just cried because the shop doesn't sell my mum's pepper soup.
quddus (talk): Oh Kemi. Homesickness is real, and almost everyone feels it in the first months.
kemi (worried): Everyone here seems fine. Maybe I made a mistake coming.
quddus (talk): Many of them are feeling the same thing, they just don't show it. It doesn't mean you made a mistake.

== cafe | WEEKEND · INTERNATIONAL CAFÉ | cozy café with flags, warm lights and people chatting | cafe
quddus (point): Try this. Keep a small routine, join one student group, and find people from home and from everywhere else.
> 2b50 | WHEN YOU MISS HOME | 1f4f1 Call home, but not all day | 1f30d Join one student group | 1f35f Find or cook food from home | 1f4ac Talk to student support
kemi (think): And if it gets really heavy?
quddus (thumbs): Talk to your university's student support or counselling team. That's what they're there for.
kemi (cheer): I found an African students' group. They're cooking pepper soup on Saturday!
